# The Library at datarail.org/library.
#
# IONOS sends no Cache-Control of its own, so a file here can be served from a
# cache for the best part of a day after it changes. For the page that is
# untidy; for apps.json it is a bug with teeth.
#
# apps.json is the grantable-apps whitelist, and the storage service reads it
# server side to decide whether an app id may be granted at all. A stale copy
# does not say "I am old", it says the app does not exist -- so an entry marked
# grantable here would be refused at the console with "the library publishes no
# app called ..." until the cache let go, and nothing anywhere would explain
# why.
#
# index.html and library.js render library.json and must not drift apart from
# it, so they revalidate on the same terms. All four are small; this costs a
# conditional request per visit and nothing when nothing changed.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(html|js|json)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
